# Typed options in the settings menu: a disabled plugin, list items, map entries added through the language picker and removed with Ctrl+d (a default one through null), the theme picker, int bounds, a multi-line text option; then the Keybinds UI and a rebind in keybinds.json.
size 90x36
config
{"lsp": {"enabled": false}, "plugins": {"markdown": {"enabled": false}}}
end
file a.txt
x
end
run a.txt
wait x
key ctrl+p
type settings open config ui
key enter
wait auto_close_pairs
type markdown.
wait markdown.enabled
snap disabled The markdown plugin is disabled: only its enabled row is listed
key ctrl+a
type languages.python.patterns
wait + add item
snap list A list shows one row per item, a header counting them and an add row
key ctrl+a
type languages.python.patterns[2]
wait *.pyw
key enter
wait languages.python.patterns[2]: *.pyw
key ctrl+a
type *.pyi
key enter
wait set to *.pyi
snap item-edited Enter edits the item in place; the whole list is written, marked as overridden
key ctrl+a
type format.commands
wait + add entry
key enter
wait format.commands >
snap language-picker Enter on a map asks for the new key with a picker of the languages
type lua
key enter
wait format.commands.lua:
type stylua -
key enter
wait format.commands.lua added
snap entry-added Then for the value; the new entry is written under its key and selected
key ctrl+d
wait format.commands.lua removed
snap entry-removed Ctrl+d removes the entry again
key ctrl+a
type format.commands.go
wait gofmt
key ctrl+d
wait format.commands.go removed
snap default-removed Ctrl+d on a default entry writes null; the entry stays listed as removed (Ctrl+d again restores it)
key ctrl+a
type theme
wait Color theme
key enter
wait theme >
snap theme-picker A choice opens a picker over its live choices (qed.theme.list)
type nord
key enter
wait theme set to nord
snap theme-set The picked theme is written and applied
key ctrl+a
type tab_width
wait Display width
key enter
wait tab_width: 4
key ctrl+a
type 0
key enter
wait at least 1
snap int-refused An int below its min is refused and nothing is written
key ctrl+a
type ai.edit_prompt
wait Edit request template
key enter
wait Ctrl+s save
snap text-box A text option opens a few-row editor box in the menu (wrapped, undo and selection like the buffer)
key enter
type Keep the answer short.
snap text-edited Enter inserts a newline; nothing is written yet
key ctrl+s
wait ai.edit_prompt set to
snap text-saved Ctrl+s writes the text; the row shows it with its newlines as \n
key esc esc
key ctrl+p
type settings open keybinds ui
key enter
wait Chord
snap keybinds-ui Settings: Open Keybinds UI opens the menu on the Keybinds tab
type toggle line wrap
wait Toggle Line Wrap
key enter
wait Press a chord
key alt+w
wait set to Alt+w
key esc esc
key ctrl+p
type settings open keybinds json
key enter
wait "toggle_line_wrap": "Alt+w"
snap rebind-file The bind is written to keybinds.json under its group ("core", or a plugin id) and the command's id
